.TH "SPEECHSYNTHESISUTTERANCE.MARK_EVENT" "3JS" "July 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SpeechSynthesisUtterance.mark_event \- SpeechSynthesisUtterance: mark
event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]mark\f[B]\f[R] event of the Web Speech API
\f[CR]SpeechSynthesisUtterance\f[R] object is fired when the spoken
utterance reaches a named SSML \(lqmark\(rq tag.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqmark\(dq, (event) => { })

onmark = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]SpeechSynthesisEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
You can use the \f[CR]mark\f[R] event in an \f[CR]addEventListener\f[R]
method:
.IP
.EX
utterThis.addEventListener(\(dqmark\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(\(gaA mark was reached: ${event.name}\(ga);
});
.EE
.PP
Or use the \f[CR]onmark\f[R] event handler property:
.IP
.EX
utterThis.onmark = (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(\(gaA mark was reached: ${event.name}\(ga);
};
.EE
